<Shell title="Start Here" section="start"><header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">YOUR FIRST PROMPT</p><h1>Start small.<br/>Get something useful.</h1><p class="lede">You don’t need design experience. Pick one screen in your website or app and one thing you want to improve.</p></header><div class="guide-layout"><ol class="start-steps"><li><h2>Choose what you want help with</h2><p>Not sure what’s wrong? Start with the free screen review. It asks the AI to explain the problems before making changes.</p><a class="button" href="/library#prompt-1">Read the screen review</a></li><li><h2>Fill in your details</h2><p>Use the customizer to add your app name, screen, audience, and goal. Text in square brackets, like <code>[APP NAME]</code>, is a placeholder for your information.</p><p class="example"><b>For example:</b> Study Planner · Signup screen · New college students · Create an account without getting confused.</p><a class="button primary" href="/builder?prompt=1">Customize my first prompt</a></li><li><h2>Copy it into your AI tool</h2><p>Select <b>Build my prompt</b>, then <b>Copy prompt</b>. Paste it into ChatGPT or Claude with a screenshot. If you use an AI coding tool, open your project there and paste the prompt into its chat.</p><p>Remove passwords and private information from screenshots or code before sharing.</p></li><li><h2>Review the result</h2><p>Look for a clear explanation of the problem and a small, practical improvement. AI can make mistakes. Check suggestions against your actual screen.</p><details><summary>What might an answer look like?</summary><p class="example"><b>Illustrative example—not a generated result:</b> “The signup button is hard to find. Make the main action more prominent and keep the secondary link quieter. Then check that both still work on a phone.”</p></details></li><li><h2>Ask for one focused follow-up</h2><p>Try: “Explain the most important issue in plain language” or “Fix only that issue and tell me how to test it.”</p><a class="button" href="/checklists">Check your changes</a></li></ol><section class="panel guide-note"><p class="tiny">GOOD TO KNOW</p><h2>You stay in control.</h2><p>This site prepares instructions. It does not run AI or change your project.</p><p><b>UI</b> means the screens and controls people use. <b>UX</b> means how clear and easy the experience feels.</p><p>Your saved prompts and notes stay in this browser. Export a backup from <a href="/toolkit">My saved work</a> to keep a copy.</p></section></div></Shell>
